WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:05.420
Flying in a plane nowadays is about as safe
as catching a ride on a bus or commuting on

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:06.420
the subway.

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:09.379
Of course, that doesn’t stop people being
afraid of flying.

00:00:09.379 --> 00:00:13.840
To some, the prospect of long-haul flights,
or feeling the shudder of turbulence, are

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:17.070
reasons to avoid planes altogether.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:22.641
And then, every year there are stories of
downed flights or those that go missing, all

00:00:22.641 --> 00:00:25.320
adding fuel to that aviophobia fire.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:31.140
Take, for example, the infamous Bermuda Triangle,
that well known region of the western part

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:33.230
of the North Atlantic Ocean.

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:35.690
What does that have to do with a fear of flying?

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:39.960
Well, famously a high number of aircraft are
believed to have mysteriously vanished while

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:45.900
flying over the Bermuda Triangle, their wreckage
and passengers rarely ever recovered.

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:49.920
Stories like that are enough to make anyone
think twice about setting foot in a plane

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:50.920
again.

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:55.000
And then, there’s SCP-787.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:58.980
As you may have already guessed, SCP-787 is
a plane.

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:02.910
Specifically, it is a Boeing 747 200.

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:07.330
With a wingspan of nearly two hundred feet,
and capable of seating over eight hundred

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:14.140
passengers, the 747 200 is part of the famous
Boeing 747 family of aircraft.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:19.120
These are quad engine commercial airliners,
designed to be the safest ever built.

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:26.480
The particular Boeing 747 200 that has since
become known by the Foundation as SCP-787

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:30.570
is slightly different from one that might
take you from your nearest airport to your

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:32.520
long awaited vacation though.

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:39.620
For one, SCP-787 has no known date of manufacture
and no call sign, both which a standard Boeing

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:42.010
aircraft would be expected to have.

00:01:42.010 --> 00:01:46.939
Additionally, the plane’s entire exterior
has been repainted; strangely, even the windows

00:01:46.939 --> 00:01:52.950
have been painted over, and the paint was
still wet when SCP-787 was first discovered.

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:54.450
As for the inner workings?

00:01:54.450 --> 00:02:00.290
All of SCP-787’s mechanical components,
including its turbines, engines and landing

00:02:00.290 --> 00:02:04.670
gear, are in perfect working order, with no
signs of any damage.

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:10.229
In fact, The SCP Foundation’s researchers
aren’t even sure that SCP-787 has actually

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:12.670
flown since its construction.

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:17.780
The plane’s machinery looks so pristine
that they might be brand new, with no detectable

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:20.230
signs of any previous use.

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:24.569
However, inside the main body of the plane
it seems to be a different story.

00:02:24.569 --> 00:02:29.290
Anything not mechanical like the carpets and
seats have decayed over time.

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:31.680
Perhaps strangest of all is the cockpit.

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:36.090
Both the pilot’s and co-pilot’s chairs
have been replaced with two masses of computer

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:39.230
components, arranged to take the shape of
two chairs.

00:02:39.230 --> 00:02:41.849
“So, what?” you might be thinking.

00:02:41.849 --> 00:02:47.629
After all, SCP-787 is, for all intents and
purposes, just an ordinary plane.

00:02:47.629 --> 00:02:50.070
Not enough to put you off flying, right?

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:54.660
Nothing more than a Boeing with a few little
things off about it like some missing seats

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:56.000
and decaying upholstery.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:02.170
Well there’s that… and then there’s
the over five hundred dead bodies on board.

00:03:02.170 --> 00:03:06.870
In June 1987, this flight of the dead was
discovered several kilometers outside of the

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:09.800
city of Bremerton in Washington State.

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:14.990
The SCP Foundation moved in, securing the
plane and swiftly getting it into containment.

00:03:14.990 --> 00:03:21.030
Now kept within a Foundation hangar, the interior
of SCP-787 is monitored for twenty-four hours

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:22.400
a day.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:26.800
Surveillance cameras and microphones are located
within the cockpit, passenger areas, and even

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:32.040
in the plane’s baggage hold, with recorded
footage and sound relayed back to the Foundation.

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:37.480
The idea of a plane filled with cadavers is
certainly unnerving, and more than a little

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:40.690
creepy, but why the need for all the surveillance?

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:43.349
After all, the bodies on board are all dead,
right?

00:03:43.349 --> 00:03:45.280
Surely, they’re not going anywhere.

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:47.720
Well, let’s talk about those bodies.

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:51.100
How would you expect someone to die when they
are aboard a plane?

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:53.739
Maybe they’d be thrown around during a crash
landing?

00:03:53.739 --> 00:03:58.140
Or perhaps a sudden depressurisation might
cause the passengers to suffocate due to a

00:03:58.140 --> 00:03:59.410
lack of oxygen?

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:01.950
Under normal circumstances, you might be right.

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:08.100
But SCP-787 is no ordinary plane, and the
passengers on board were not killed in ways

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:12.260
you might expect for an ordinary aircraft
accident.

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:18.169
Referred to by research staff as SCP-787a
specimens, the cadavers aboard this particular

00:04:18.169 --> 00:04:23.110
Boeing 747 200 all have dramatically different
causes of death.

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:28.400
Some of the specimens show signs of strangulation,
others seem to have starved or drowned.

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:33.330
Other bodies on board have injuries like gunshot
or stab wounds, while further corpses look

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:36.270
to have died as a result of blunt force trauma.

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:41.879
A few have even been exsanguinated, that is,
completely drained of all their blood.

00:04:41.879 --> 00:04:47.800
One commonality among all the specimens on
board SCP-787 is that some form of mutilation

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:49.050
has occurred.

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:53.529
Twenty-three passengers had their tongues
removed, a further seventy-three were scalped,

00:04:53.529 --> 00:04:58.300
230 had Cyrillic letters carved into their
left hands and almost five hundred of the

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:00.990
passengers had their fingertips removed.

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:03.099
Let’s recap what we have so far.

00:05:03.099 --> 00:05:07.530
First, there’s a Boeing 747 200 found randomly
sitting in a field.

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:11.629
Second, it’s filled with over five hundred
mutilated bodies.

00:05:11.629 --> 00:05:16.050
And third, each one appears to have died from
a cause you wouldn’t typically expect of

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:18.020
an airline accident.

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:23.719
Seems strange enough, but of course then there’s
the apparitions and noises that manifest inside

00:05:23.719 --> 00:05:29.360
SCP-787, which is why the Foundation keeps
the plane under round-the-clock surveillance

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:34.129
so they can monitor any anomalous activity
taking place aboard this flight of the dead.

00:05:34.129 --> 00:05:38.350
Any attempts by Foundation personnel to enter
the plane during an anomalous occurrence have

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:44.189
led to individuals being physically ejected
from SCP-787, causing severe organ damage

00:05:44.189 --> 00:05:47.860
and internal bleeding for up to seventy-two
hours.

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:53.720
The anomalies that occur inside SCP-787 range
from the presence of loud noises with no obvious

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:58.229
source, to the manifestation of strange human-shaped
entities within the plane.

00:05:58.229 --> 00:06:04.490
The first anomalous occurrence recorded within
SCP-787 was in 1988, when the sound of a loud

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:08.660
pounding was heard against the doors and windows
of the plane’s left side.

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:13.300
Two years later, a male voice could be heard
from the onboard bathroom, repeating a singular

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:19.610
phrase over and over: “Philosophers always
run from the advanced thickening treatment”.

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:25.009
In 1993, the plane’s in-flight entertainment
system seemed to be activated by itself.

00:06:25.009 --> 00:06:29.199
The overhead screens showed a bizarre choice
of in-flight movie: colorless pictures of

00:06:29.199 --> 00:06:34.370
a deceased man, accompanied by a female voice
reading a gynaecology book in Czech.

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:39.569
The same year, the longest lasting of the
SCP-787 anomalies took place.

00:06:39.569 --> 00:06:44.540
This time, the plane’s “Fasten Seatbelts”
sign spent almost four hours flickering, while

00:06:44.540 --> 00:06:49.659
the first fifteen seconds of Jefferson Airplane’s
White Rabbit played on a loop over the onboard

00:06:49.659 --> 00:06:50.659
speakers.

00:06:50.659 --> 00:06:57.800
It wasn’t until 1997 that the first of the
humanoid entities appeared aboard SCP-787.

00:06:57.800 --> 00:07:03.479
This figure was indistinct, lacking any discernible
detail, little more than just a human shape

00:07:03.479 --> 00:07:05.240
standing in the aisles.

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:09.259
Observed by the Foundation’s surveillance
equipment, the figure was seen removing an

00:07:09.259 --> 00:07:13.550
emergency oxygen supply and mask from seat
H43.

00:07:13.550 --> 00:07:18.449
It stood perfectly still, wearing the passenger’s
breathing mask for over two minutes before

00:07:18.449 --> 00:07:23.379
removing the mask and disappearing from the
view of the cameras placed onboard.

00:07:23.379 --> 00:07:27.610
The figure did not appear anywhere else inside
the plane.

00:07:27.610 --> 00:07:32.360
Another figure appeared four years later in
2001, sitting in the mass of computer parts

00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:34.669
that made up the co-pilot’s chair.

00:07:34.669 --> 00:07:38.839
This figure, much like its predecessor, was
indistinct in its features.

00:07:38.839 --> 00:07:45.419
For almost four minutes, it sat in the cockpit
of the Boeing 747 200, just whimpering softly.

00:07:45.419 --> 00:07:49.839
Then, it lurched forward, vomiting all over
the console in front of it, before quickly

00:07:49.839 --> 00:07:51.819
disappearing like the first figure.

00:07:51.819 --> 00:07:56.439
SCP Foundation personnel collected a sample
of the vomit that the entity left behind.

00:07:56.439 --> 00:08:01.399
After performing an analysis of the sample,
research staff found traces of nitrous oxide,

00:08:01.399 --> 00:08:05.169
thorium, bird droppings… and three human
fingernails.

00:08:05.169 --> 00:08:09.839
At present, the origin of these humanoid figures
is still unknown.

00:08:09.839 --> 00:08:14.429
Could these entities be the souls of the dead
passengers, trying to offer insight into what

00:08:14.429 --> 00:08:15.909
happened aboard this flight?

00:08:15.909 --> 00:08:20.219
Or perhaps these indistinct, human-shaped
creatures are the ones responsible for the

00:08:20.219 --> 00:08:23.719
deaths of SCP-787’s passengers?

00:08:23.719 --> 00:08:30.229
The next anomaly within SCP-787 occurred in
2005, when a female voice was recorded speaking

00:08:30.229 --> 00:08:32.300
through the onboard speaker system.

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:37.300
The voice said: “For your comfort and enjoyment
today, pancakes will now be served.

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:39.639
Please do not leave your seat.

00:08:39.639 --> 00:08:41.069
Pancakes will now be served.

00:08:41.069 --> 00:08:42.959
Please do not leave your seat.

00:08:42.959 --> 00:08:44.699
Do not leave your seat.

00:08:44.699 --> 00:08:46.089
Leave your seat.

00:08:46.089 --> 00:08:47.089
Please.

00:08:47.089 --> 00:08:48.730
Pancakes will now be served.

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:51.000
Yaaaaaaaaaaaay pancakes!”

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:54.959
Exactly what the relevance of pancakes are
to the plane full of bodies is still under

00:08:54.959 --> 00:08:57.790
investigation by the SCP Foundation.

00:08:57.790 --> 00:09:03.560
Next, in 2007, the Boeing’s overhead emergency
air masks fell from the ceiling, only to be

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:05.210
snatched back upwards.

00:09:05.210 --> 00:09:09.779
They continued deploying and retracting for
fourteen minutes, while the plane was simultaneously

00:09:09.779 --> 00:09:12.000
filled with the noise of screams.

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:16.860
Finally, the only other notable anomaly took
place a year later, when the onboard temperature

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:23.379
within SCP-787 dropped thirty-three degrees,
from twenty to minus thirteen Celsius in a

00:09:23.379 --> 00:09:24.860
matter of seconds.

00:09:24.860 --> 00:09:29.629
By the late 2000s, the SCP Foundation’s
researchers were having little luck understanding

00:09:29.629 --> 00:09:32.529
the nature of SCP-787’s anomalies.

00:09:32.529 --> 00:09:38.029
Instead, they turned their attention to identifying
the bodies of the deceased passengers onboard.

00:09:38.029 --> 00:09:42.779
Through the use of advanced forensics and
population databases, these researchers attempted

00:09:42.779 --> 00:09:46.850
to determine where exactly these bodies had
come from.

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:50.279
Researchers still hadn’t determined if they
had all died on the plane, or if someone had

00:09:50.279 --> 00:09:54.579
exhumed them from graves before placing them
aboard for some unknown reason.

00:09:54.579 --> 00:09:56.740
In fact, the answer was neither.

00:09:56.740 --> 00:10:02.310
And Foundation researchers discovered something
that no-one had expected: One of the passengers

00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:03.769
was still alive.

00:10:03.769 --> 00:10:09.490
To clarify, the body aboard SCP-787 was definitely
still deceased.

00:10:09.490 --> 00:10:13.899
But researchers identified the cadaver as
a retired optometrist from Atlanta, Georgia,

00:10:13.899 --> 00:10:16.540
who was still very much alive.

00:10:16.540 --> 00:10:21.069
Foundation agents found that the man was simultaneously
alive and well at his Atlanta home, but also

00:10:21.069 --> 00:10:24.360
dead on-board the Boeing 747 200.

00:10:24.360 --> 00:10:28.380
The subject was interviewed by agents, and
had no prior knowledge of any incident taking

00:10:28.380 --> 00:10:34.139
place in June 1987 when SCP-787 was first
discovered.

00:10:34.139 --> 00:10:38.480
Even more interestingly, he claimed that he’d
never even set foot aboard an airplane, which

00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:41.379
his wife and son both confirmed to be true.

00:10:41.379 --> 00:10:42.810
So, what does this mean?

00:10:42.810 --> 00:10:48.850
How could the same man have been alive in
Georgia and dead aboard SCP-787?

00:10:48.850 --> 00:10:53.540
Perhaps the answer can be found in a surprising
place… the plane’s toilet.

00:10:53.540 --> 00:10:58.509
Or to be more specific, the place where things
flushed in the toilet go to.

00:10:58.509 --> 00:11:02.971
Examinations of the airplane’s waste storage
tank revealed something very surprising, there

00:11:02.971 --> 00:11:07.850
was one more SCP-787a specimen that had been
overlooked.

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:12.040
It is unknown just how he got in there, but
researchers discovered the body of an Indian

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:14.310
man who looked to be in his thirties.

00:11:14.310 --> 00:11:18.649
The man, who was wearing a three piece suit,
was found to be carrying a number of puzzling

00:11:18.649 --> 00:11:25.160
items, including a surgical mask and gloves,
an unloaded Beretta DT-10 shotgun, several

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:30.080
cinnamon flavored mints, a switchblade knife,
an amulet that appears to depict the Eye of

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:35.250
Horus, and a ticket stub for the Return of
the Jedi with the number “92” written

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:36.430
on the back.

00:11:36.430 --> 00:11:40.629
All of these objects seem to be completely
random, and the Foundation has been unable

00:11:40.629 --> 00:11:45.420
to make sense of what they were doing on the
man, or why his body does not seem to show

00:11:45.420 --> 00:11:49.230
the same state of decay as the rest of those
found on board.

00:11:49.230 --> 00:11:52.190
There was one item that may hold some answers
though.

00:11:52.190 --> 00:11:57.870
For some reason this man also possessed a
copy of SCP-787’s flight log.

00:11:57.870 --> 00:12:03.839
The log consisted of a series of coordinates
which were repeated 5,478 times.

00:12:03.839 --> 00:12:08.120
The coordinates point to a seemingly random
spot in the Pacific ocean, several hundred

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:12.760
miles away from the infamous Pitcairn Islands,
the island that the famous mutineers of the

00:12:12.760 --> 00:12:17.259
HMS Bounty settled after taking over their
ship and leaving the captain adrift on the

00:12:17.259 --> 00:12:18.259
ocean.

00:12:18.259 --> 00:12:21.720
Is this location the secret to SCP-787?

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:26.660
While none of this is confirmed, nor denied,
by anyone at the SCP Foundation, one theory

00:12:26.660 --> 00:12:31.829
surrounding the area is that the location
is another Bermuda Triangle like location,

00:12:31.829 --> 00:12:36.620
one that contains some sort of temporal anomaly
that unwitting planes fly through, only to

00:12:36.620 --> 00:12:39.259
find themselves displaced in time.

00:12:39.259 --> 00:12:42.779
Of course, the problem with that theory is
that the man from Atlanta said he’d never

00:12:42.779 --> 00:12:44.339
been aboard a plane before.

00:12:44.339 --> 00:12:46.829
Or, at least not yet.

00:12:46.829 --> 00:12:51.930
It is entirely possible that SCP-787 is a
plane that made a flight at some point in

00:12:51.930 --> 00:12:57.680
the not too distant future, only to arrive
back in June 1987 by passing through a temporal

00:12:57.680 --> 00:13:00.040
breach in the area near the Pitcairn Islands.

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:04.800
Sure, it might not explain what happened to
everyone onboard, but it could at least explain

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:08.940
how SCP-787 arrived where and when it did.

00:13:08.940 --> 00:13:13.620
Every plane is fitted with a device that records
flight data, in the event of a crash or other

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:18.579
accident, known to most as the plane’s black
box, and researchers were able to uncover

00:13:18.579 --> 00:13:23.010
SCP-787’s inside a compartment under one
of the plane’s seats.

00:13:23.010 --> 00:13:27.870
The recorder was found within a compartment
filled with toxic asbestos and dried human

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:28.870
blood.

00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:34.009
They hoped that perhaps it would contain some
answers as to where exactly SCP-787 had come

00:13:34.009 --> 00:13:37.220
from, and what had happened to its passengers.

00:13:37.220 --> 00:13:42.709
Sadly not, the flight data recorder contained
no information besides one simple phrase:

00:13:42.709 --> 00:13:44.269
“TO BE SORRY.”

00:13:44.269 --> 00:13:50.160
While an inexplicable mystery, SCP-787 is
at least classed as a Safe anomaly by the

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:54.999
Foundation, seeing as it poses no realistic
threat or shows signs of trying to break out

00:13:54.999 --> 00:13:56.220
of containment.

00:13:56.220 --> 00:14:00.540
The aircraft has only ever caused harm to
anyone trying to enter during one of its sporadic

00:14:00.540 --> 00:14:05.589
anomalous events, but apart from that, it
sits gathering dust in a hanger, just waiting

00:14:05.589 --> 00:14:08.129
for someone to crack its secrets.

00:14:08.129 --> 00:14:12.360
And who knows, maybe one day you’ll be sitting
on a plane that’s taking you to your South

00:14:12.360 --> 00:14:17.410
Pacific vacation, and the retired optometrist
sitting next to you will remark that you’re

00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:22.920
passing over the Pitcairn Islands, and you’ll
discover for yourself exactly what happened

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:25.470
to SCP-787.

00:14:25.470 --> 00:14:31.519
Now check out “SCP-354 - The Red Pool”
and “SCP-3999 - I Am At The Center of Everything

00:14:31.519 --> 00:14:35.440
That Happens To Me” for more frightening
mysteries from the SCP Foundation!

